<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suro of Geumgwan Gaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 42–199 CE (traditional)</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Kim Suro, King Suro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suro is the legendary founder of Geumgwan Gaya, the leading state of the Gaya confederacy in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gimhae">Gimhae</a>. According to tradition he hatched from a golden egg sent from heaven in 42 CE and married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heo-hwang-ok">Heo Hwang-ok</a>, a princess from a distant land. He is honoured as the ancestor of the Gimhae Kim clan, Korea's largest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suro-of-geumgwan-gaya.jpg" alt="Suro of Geumgwan Gaya" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This file is a Work of Kwj2772 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suro_Tomb.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
